 "col_note": "<id>_col.glb: collision only, nodes named colNNNN-colonly (Godot imports StaticBody3D + shape, no mesh). Same origin as the visual GLB. Built from a 0.5 m column grid (heights snapped to 0.25 m), roofed interiors solid, each door has a walk-in opening >=1.4 m wide x >=2.3 m tall (see door_points[].opening) cut ~1.5 m deep, with low steps in front removed. door_points: pos (door threshold, metres, building space), normal/yaw_deg = outward facing (yaw 0 = +Z).",
 "phone_note": "phone_high_lod = which file the phone High tier should load (lod1 = the _lod1 file). Medium/Low phone tiers step down one more level. All heavy buildings: lod1 <= ~47-50% of High tris, lod2 <= ~19-20%."
}